{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":408195,"ns":0,"title":"Cauchy principal value","extract":"In mathematics, the Cauchy principal value, named after Augustin-Louis Cauchy, is a method for assigning values to certain improper integrals which would otherwise be undefined. In this method, a singularity on an integral interval is avoided by limiting the integral interval to the non-singular domain.","description":"Method for assigning values to integrals","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}